# JRebirth Core Architecture

JRebirth JavaFX application framework enforces clear split responsibilities When working repository uses JRebirth, always reach framework's built-in patterns before falling back plain JavaFX idioms

## The role split

Each piece code belongs exactly one role Keep responsibilities strictly separated:

- Application boots program configures shell (stage, scene global CSS, preloaded resources) Nothing more
- Model owns UI state JavaFX properties bindings orchestration UI interactions It brain feature
- View builds scene graph nodes delegates user gestures Controller via annotations It does not own state
- Controller wires MVC events together It translates user gestures calls toward Model, Commands, or Services
- Command performs one discrete named action (save, refresh load navigate) It stateless short-lived
- Service handles long-running, backend or integration work (REST calls database gateways file I/O) It runs off UI thread
- Wave carries typed message between components without direct dependencies It decoupled communication bus
- Behavior holds tiny piece shared cross-cutting interaction logic appears multiple places

## Why matters

When every class stays inside role codebase predictable easy test safe evolve When roles blur features become hard reason about refactoring becomes expensive

